<figure
  class="quality-lifecycle"
  aria-labelledby="quality-lifecycle-caption"
  aria-describedby="quality-lifecycle-text"
>
  <p id="quality-lifecycle-text" class="lifecycle-text">
    A seven-stage sequence connects shared rule meaning, reusable analytical checks,
    management and technical reporting, owner routing, source correction outside the
    audit, cycle comparison, and continued visibility of unresolved issues and
    regressions.
  </p>
  <p class="sequence-cue">Follow stages 01–07.</p>
  <ol class="quality-process">
    <li class="shared-stage">
      <span class="stage-type">Shared definition</span>
      <strong>Confirm rule meaning and responsible owner</strong>
      <small>
        Agree what the check means and who can interpret or correct a finding.
      </small>
    </li>
    <li class="audit-stage">
      <span class="stage-type">Analytical audit</span>
      <strong>Run reusable validation checks</strong>
      <small>
        Apply the configured rules and keep missing or exceptional inputs visible.
      </small>
    </li>
    <li class="audit-stage">
      <span class="stage-type">Analytical audit</span>
      <strong>Produce a health summary and exception package</strong>
      <small>Provide a management view and the detail needed for investigation.</small>
    </li>
    <li class="shared-stage">
      <span class="stage-type">Shared review</span>
      <strong>Classify and route findings</strong>
      <small>
        Send each finding to the owner with the authority and context to respond.
      </small>
    </li>
    <li class="owner-stage">
      <span class="stage-type">Owner-led remediation</span>
      <strong>Correct the source outside the audit framework</strong>
      <small>Keep source changes under the control of the responsible owner.</small>
    </li>
    <li class="audit-stage">
      <span class="stage-type">Analytical audit</span>
      <strong>Re-run and compare audit cycles</strong>
      <small>
        Distinguish corrected findings from issues that remain or newly appear.
      </small>
    </li>
    <li class="shared-stage">
      <span class="stage-type">Continuing review</span>
      <strong>Retain unresolved issues and newly detected regressions</strong>
      <small>
        Carry open findings forward instead of resetting the record each cycle.
      </small>
    </li>
  </ol>
  <div class="track-key" role="group" aria-label="Lifecycle responsibility key">
    <span>
      <b>Analytical audit</b> evaluates and reports.
    </span>
    <span>
      <b>Owner-led remediation</b> changes the source.
    </span>
    <span>
      <b>Shared review</b> connects meaning, routing, and follow-up.
    </span>
  </div>
  <figcaption id="quality-lifecycle-caption" class="caption">
    A data-free lifecycle separating analytical audit work from owner-led source
    correction. Numbering, responsibility labels, headings, and descriptions communicate
    the sequence without relying on color.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

